# Publication and language

Develop this repository privately. After the competition deadline, choose between making this repository public with its history, or copying the full intended release into a fresh public repository while keeping intermediate Git history private.

Either route preserves rejected candidates, earlier versions, disagreements, failures, and the retained logs as part of the release.

## Language

- Editorial writing, methodology, navigation, and biographies are in English.
- Original conversations and prompts keep their exact language, spelling, punctuation, and profanity.
- Selected Russian quotations have separate English translations and links to their full messages.
- The five originally Russian essays are an explicit exception: preserve the Russian originals and place English reading translations beside them.
- The Russian retrospective dossier remains local working material. It is excluded from the current repository tree. An earlier private commit contained it; removing it here does not rewrite that private Git history.

## Editorial copies

Repository updates create export copies and English reading material. The local archive retains the canonical manuscripts and earlier assessments. New translations are labeled as later editorial artifacts, distinct from the versions evaluated at midterm.

Private editorial work can continue while the [selection](docs/selection.md) develops. Public release and competition submission remain separate decisions.
